      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "According to the problem:\nAfter filling all the oxygen in a 5.7 liter container, the volume is increased to 5.7 liters due to the expansion, i.e., V₂ = 5.7, and the pressure is reduced to 50% of its original value, i.e., P₁= 5 kPa, V₁=2.28. According to the formula for inverse proportionality between pressure and volume, P₂(P₁/P₂) = V₁(V₂/V₁). Substituting the given values, we get that (P₂/P₁) = V₂(V₁/V₁). This proportionality gives us the new pressure as 3.3 kPa\n5000P₂/5000P₁ = 5.7L/(2.28 L) P₂ = (5/5.7)P₁ P₂ = (5 / 5.7) * 5 P₂ = 3.3 kPa\nThus, the final pressure of the gas in the new container is 3.3 kPa.",
