      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that the pressure (P) and volume (V) of a gas are inversely proportional, we can use the formula that states \\( P \\times V = k \\) (a constant).\n\n1. Start by calculating the constant (k) using the initial conditions:\n\\[ k = P \\times V = 5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\times 2.28 \\, \\text{liter} \\]\n\\[ k = 11.4 \\, \\text{kPa \\cdot liter} \\]\n\n2. Next, we want to find the new pressure (P') when the volume changes to 5.7 liters:\n\\[ P' \\times V' = k \\]\n\\[ P' \\times 5.7 \\, liter = 11.4 \\, kPa \\cdot liter \\]\n\n3. To solve for P', we divide both sides of the equation by 5.7 liters:\n\\[ \\frac{P' \\times 5.7 \\, liter}{5.7 \\, liter} = \\frac{11.4 \\, kPa \\cdot liter}{5.7 \\, liter} \\]\n\\[ P' = \\frac{11.4}{5.7} \\, kPa \\]\n\\[ P' = 2 \\, kPa \\]\n\nTherefore, the new pressure in the 5.7 liter container will be \\boxed{2} kPa.",
